      "id": 999,
      "options": {
        "code": {
          "language": "plaintext",
          "showLineNumbers": false,
          "showMiniMap": false
        },
        "content": "### How to read this dashboard\n- **Primary filter** is **$job** (server), sourced from Loki's `job` label restricted to Minecraft log streams (`exporter=\"OTLP\"`). **$level** filters by detected log level (`detected_level`).\n- **Note:** servers are migrating their job label from bare names (e.g. `TeamBuild`) to `minecraft/<name>` (Paper/Minestom) or `proxy/<name>` (Velocity). The **$job** dropdown always shows and selects the bare name (prefix stripped), and the Loki queries below match either form or none. Tempo's `service.name` and the spanmetrics `service` label never carry this prefix, so the Tempo/spanmetrics panels (error rate, latency, top spans, trace search, slow traces) match on the same bare **$job** value automatically - no reselection needed.\n- **Logs** come from Loki (uid `loki`), **traces** from Tempo (uid `tempo`), and Tempo's span-metrics/service-graph output from Mimir (uid `mimir`) via the metrics-generator.\n- The recurring error **\"An error occurred whilst writing samples to Prometheus\" / `UnknownHostException: database01.onelite.feather`** is known baseline noise (a dead Prometheus pushgateway target) that dominates error counts on some servers - it is intentionally not alerted on. See the recurring error patterns panel below.",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "pluginVersion": "12.3.1",
      "title": "Read me first",
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "collapsed": false,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "id": 1,
      "panels": [],
      "title": "Critical",
      "type": "row"
    },
